WEBVTT

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.180
Orichalt has been put in containment.
Maintaining its stability.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.480
Begin observation with both methods.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.200
How pure is the Orichalt?
Hurry up and report.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.070
Considering the decay progress,
its estimated purity is 52.4%.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:19.860
Tch.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.870
It shouldn't be that low.
Measure it once again!

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:26.500
The return investment of this kind of Orichalt is less than 10%.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.950
It's not even worth considering!

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.700
But chief, we've measured it several times.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.750
Do you want to look for a new
job here in the sticks?

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.380
I-I'll keep observing.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:36.590
Hmph.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.250
Useless idiots.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.180
We're behind schedule, too.
We have to work faster.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:52.710
<i>Back then</i>

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:57.290
<i>I was obsessed with my job in fund management, where
I could freely move around with enough money</i>

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:00.780
<i>to influence the federation's economy. </i>

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:05.920
<i>I believed that it was something exceptional that couldn't be done without my talents.</i>

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.260
<i>But...</i>

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:11.410
There's an abnormality in the
Orichalt compressor!

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:12.810
What about the emergency
response units?

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.710
In the early stages seven people
uninstalled them!

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.090
What we're you thinking?

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.510
Detecting gravity waves!
They're growing larger

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:19.650
All hands, retreat!

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.460
We won't make it!

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.280
It's a partial warp phenomenon!

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.360
My body...

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.070
Where is my body?!

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.000
There is something...

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.950
that I can get back.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:21.060
This is a follow-up report on the sudden large-scale Miguel Net outage

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.610
that occurred at Federation
Standard Time 0043.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:29.900
After consulting with the specialists, the Government
Press Secretary announced to the press that

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.160
the estimated range of the Miguel Net outage,

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:38.440
at worst, may stretch up to 30 light
years around Fifth.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:45.280
Also, the Federation Safety Committee that urgently convened has dispatched a special investigation group.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:48.450
However, with Miguel Jumps being unusable,

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:52.620
it may take them more than eight years to reach the area around Fifth.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.500
For now, I took some measures.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:00.420
Was that a good enough cover-up to use for information control?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.220
That's a big help.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.940
It's because I didn't have enough power!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:18.480
Listen, I think there are interstellar ships that escaped from Fifth.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:22.750
We just have to buy time
until we can use that.

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:26.140
That said, the amount of Orichalt...

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:30.200
Preparations are underway to collect it across all federation planets.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:35.130
Are you serious? If you do that,
the economy will collapse.

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:38.530
No, things are already in motion.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:43.800
For the survival of humanity we have to defeat Amatsu Mikaboshi, wandering planet Rajeev.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:48.400
You're trying to do the same
that he tried to, aren't you.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.150
The same?

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:53.320
No way!

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:57.690
I have a just duty!
And the resolve to fulfill it!

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:02.820
Because the savior of humanity is me!

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:16.580
Um.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.130
Isn't there anything we can do?

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:22.370
Like what?

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.220
The scale is too large.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.530
It difficult enough uncovering the plans
of the federation's higher-ups.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.830
We're just diggers, after all.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.980
But...

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:33.270
The federation army...

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.400
The army deceived us and tried
to retrieve the Orichalt.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.860
Why talk about this now?

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:42.690
The army went only after the Orichalt.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:46.150
And they didn't know about Alice. Yet...

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.830
Observer's Sam Taylor tried
to take Alice off this ship.

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:55.580
I can only think of a midway change of
plans after they learned about Alice.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.660
What are you trying to say, Ido?

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:01.260
Sam Taylor said this to me
before he died.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.260
"Impossible! You were alive?!"

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.160
Huh?

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:05.880
That's right. He did say that.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:11.170
So that means he must of
known who Ido was, then?

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.970
Yeah. And what's more...

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:17.390
Sam Taylor and Kain Arisugawa
are like two peas in a pod.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.360
Analyzing the image,

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.070
the similarity is over 90%.

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:24.280
It's almost the same person!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:30.570
But Kain Arisugawa was born in Federation Year 39. He's 50 now.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:34.950
Even if he used advanced anti-aging measures, to look this young...

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:37.340
This Sam fella must be a clone.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:38.420
I think so, too.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:42.420
Clone technology is banned under federation law. Which means...

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.960
Yeah. It's the work of someone in power who operates outside the law.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.470
But that's no reason to pull back.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:53.100
Ido, my boy, just what did
you do back then?

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.010
That's what I want to know,
more than anyone.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:06:57.600
Huh?

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.520
I figured out Kain Arisugawa's whereabouts.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.590
Colony planet Sixth.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:08.860
Kain Arisugawa is the CEO of MT Industries,
and a laboratory of theirs is in its orbit.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.870
Ms. Karla, you were still gathering intel?

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.020
Yeah. What better chance than
a large-scale outage?

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:16.870
As expected.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:21.230
Clair, set our course for
Sixth after the briefing.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:22.060
Yep.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.960
Grayman, my opinion is just a theory-

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.010
But it's not like there's no chance.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:31.640
And we're not patient enough to just
sit quiet and watch how things go.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.390
So, well, why don't we go meet him?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.890
That Kain Arisugawa guy.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:38.890
Grayman.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:41.690
Isn't that just fine?
There's nothing else to do. Right?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.980
I know.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:45.400
Let's go to Sixth, Mr. Ido!

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.410
Mr. Ido!

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.950
Jeez, you guys...

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:02.560
So, at what point shall we dig?

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.240
Let's do TR45.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:05.770
Change that to TR47.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:06.550
Huh?

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.420
Who're you?

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.110
Karla Milla-Foden.

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:13.180
I came to offer my intelligence
gathering skills.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:18.960
The probability of high-grade
Orichalt in TR47 is 92.7%.

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:22.390
If you want to make money,
go dig that. Right now.

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.600
Hmph, then do it yourself!

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.650
You can have the treasure if it's there.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.630
Are you making fun of my intel?!

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.530
You're just miners in the
middle of nowhere.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.440
Your information may be accurate.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.940
But who'd believe someone who's
speaking in that kind of tone?

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.240
Where's the logic here?

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.940
I'm saying that I can't put my life in the hands of someone I don't trust!

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:45.680
Can't you understand
something so simple?!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:50.880
I really am a terrible woman.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:57.300
Hmm, I'd like to head
directly to Sixth, but...

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.000
We can't let ourselves get
ambushed by the army.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.050
This will take time, but should
we use short jumps?

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:05.400
Karla! Can you calculate the route?

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:09.520
Yes. This is a route made by buying
the rights to Miguel Jumps.

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:14.600
Bought from fellow miners, illegal merchants
and such, so nobody will report us to the army.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:17.190
You've sure done a lot over such a short time.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.160
Tricks of my trade.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:20.580
Clair, jump along the route.

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:21.680
Sure.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:23.750
Initiating Miguel Jump sequence.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:26.880
Deploying spatial mesh using
Vega as the reference point.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.040
Unit of measurement: AU.

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:30.460
Putting this ship in grid 1
Alice, you can come out now.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.700
Deploying grid 2 in the same space.

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.540
Time until the Orichalt is released from the containment mechanism.

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:37.390
10...

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:38.560
9...

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:39.560
8...

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:40.580
7...

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:41.560
6...

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.600
5...

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:42.610
Will I learn about my past if I meet him?

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:43.570
4...

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:44.560
3...

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:45.570
2...

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:46.570
1...

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:46.580
Will I learn about my past if I meet him?

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.460
Containment mechanism, stopped.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:49.900
Orichalt, released.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.560
Don't be afraid.

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:58.440
I can do it.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:01.290
I am the being that can protect mankind!

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:05.290
And for that I have to confirm it.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.780
The truth behind the mercy
during the old days.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.210
Jump complete.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.510
Starting the second sequence after
confirming the coordinates.

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:18.960
Huh?

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.660
Boss, that's!

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:21.650
What?

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:24.060
That's Escavate...

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.890
Hey, Grayman!

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.560
Papa, it's Denrai's president.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.310
Oh, it's been a while, Sacchan.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:36.070
What did you do? Everyone in
the business was contacted.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.280
Told us to report immediately
if we see you.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:41.870
We got caught in a bit of trouble.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.360
What the hell.

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:46.920
I won't tell anyone you were here,
but I don't want any trouble either.

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:48.420
So hurry up and be on your way.

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.650
Hehe, we're in your debt!

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:02.850
After 12 more jumps we'll
be at the edge of Sixth.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:06.850
It's surprising that the army didn't
interfere, or, rather, disappointing.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:09.130
They're probably busy 'cause of Fifth.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.620
When the army captured all of you,
I looked through the personal files.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:17.530
Sixth is your home, right?
And your body's also there?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:18.240
Not there.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.070
Where is it, then?

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:21.880
Dismantled.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:24.080
Total paralysis after an accident.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:27.580
It ended up being declared brain dead
and it was immediately disposed of.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:31.500
But then when did you
Mind Trance into this body?

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.340
Oh? What? You wanna know?

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:35.830
Just tell me already.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:37.200
All right, sure.

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:39.980
Asteroid Speed pilots

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:45.120
copy their consciousness into the machines and
both simultaneously process the information.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.640
And I'm the copy.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:50.980
So that's a backup data in case
something happens?!

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:53.230
And you never had a body
to begin with?!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:56.490
Yep. Just like a ghost, right?

00:11:56.490 --> 00:12:00.690
I'm Rick Ayer, and yet I'm not Rick Ayer.

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:04.740
That's why you don't use a human
avatar in the expanded space?

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.360
You could say that's where I draw the line?

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:11.740
Yeah, even after becoming
like this I still...

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:13.390
You still want to race?

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.510
After women, too.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.690
Says a machine.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:22.130
This is what you wanted to talk
about before we reach Sixth?

00:12:22.780 --> 00:12:24.360
Listen, Amanza.

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:30.140
Am I alive?
Or am I a virtual personality?

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:35.780
At least, you exist right here.

00:12:35.780 --> 00:12:37.690
Exist right here, huh...

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.070
Saved by your words.

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.460
Short jump completed.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.120
The overall sequence is over.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.250
We've entered Sixth's sector.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:54.620
Good.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.530
Alice, we reached Sixth.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.390
The army's on standby at the
other side of the orbit, huh.

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:04.380
To think there was a jump-worthy
Orichalt in this place.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:09.430
I scared Zepher who fed us fake
intel into putting it there.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:13.260
He made us go through hell,
this much is only natural.

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:15.930
Can't anger the women, right?

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:19.950
Well, what do we do, Ido?
Stulti might stand out.

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:22.570
Only a select few of us will go.
Me and...

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:25.410
Gotta have me there to
collect the data.

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:27.130
That's right.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:29.990
Then, Maya who's good at astrogeology.

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:30.740
Eh?

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.870
And we'll also take Alice.

00:13:33.140 --> 00:13:34.410
Alice, too?

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:38.410
It's possible that Kain Arisugawa
knows what exactly is Alice.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.350
So you're leaving us behind?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.520
Provide backup.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:45.960
Worst case, there will be fighting.
We'll need reinforcements.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.760
All right, Roger Wilco!

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.640
Ah! That's my phrase!

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.640
It's mine now!

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.400
Rick!

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:53.970
What's up, my pumpkin?

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:58.730
I understand you're nervous before an
operation with a proper plan for once, but...

00:13:58.730 --> 00:13:59.650
It's unsightly.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:00.820
Sorry.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.900
We're ready.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:12.300
Sis, take care of Ido and our girl.

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.810
I mean, who knows what they'd do
if left on their own.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.460
Grave responsibility, isn't it.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.380
Be careful, Ido.
Don't go too far.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:20.700
Got it.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:23.530
I hope you'll learn about your past.

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:25.530
Thanks, Clair.

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.640
Well... I'll be back.

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:38.980
"Thanks". Ido has changed a bit?

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.860
Or that's how he originally was,
it would seem.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:48.310
I've disguised all of our life signatures
as MT Industries staff.

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:50.160
We should be able to easily get in.

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.130
You can even do that.

00:14:52.130 --> 00:15:00.170
Maya, according to Karla's intel the MT Industries facility
is barrier-free, I-Machines can freely move around, but...

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.750
If something happens, we'll be relying on you.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:06.590
Understood. I'll just need to bring
Kain Arisugawa, right?

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.110
I'm counting on you.

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:20.980
I see it. It's MT Industries.

00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:23.260
Just how huge is it.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:26.400
As expected of a company that invented the Mind Trance System, I guess.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:30.380
Just proof of how much they're filling their pockets thanks to the stupidly expensive patent fees.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:35.170
But without the MT System we wouldn't have been able to keep living.

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:37.720
So we should be grateful
in that respect, huh.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:42.790
Mr. Ido, the facility approved
our identities. No problems.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:45.960
We'll enter through the central gate.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.120
To think we're just easily
coming in like this.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:57.850
That's thanks to Zepher.

00:15:57.850 --> 00:15:59.940
Where's Kain Arisugawa?

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:03.340
Probably in the lab in the
sector with gravity.

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:05.650
We'll need to pass through
the hatch to the right.

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.410
Did we reach the gravity zone?

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:26.130
There's even air.
What a cutting-edge facility.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.560
T-This is...

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:41.320
Rather than a lab this looks
like an entire city!

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:42.390
Yeah.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.390
Where's Kain Arisugawa's room?

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:47.360
According to the intel it's
on the other side, but...

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:51.610
It's an M-class scale facility, it's not like we can just walk there.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:54.060
There shouldn't be any gravity
in the center.

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:55.960
So we can fly there.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.780
Maya, brace for impact.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:58.870
Right.

00:17:17.250 --> 00:17:19.070
Nobody's here?

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:22.980
Security?!

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:31.970
The informer didn't know
about this, did they.

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:33.490
Who knows.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.490
Karla...

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.910
Ms. Karla, what's going on?

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:46.920
I'm sorry. But there's something I need to take back, no matter what, Ido.

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.670
It doesn't matter.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:55.260
The course to Sixth, the infiltration of this
facility, there's been too little interference.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.760
I expected something like
this could happen.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.540
If you knew it,
why didn't you stop me?

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:03.930
I don't have a past.
Neither do I know my family.

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:09.400
So I should at least trust bonds
of comradeship, right?

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:12.070
Even if it's just a business relationship?

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.280
I guess, so!

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:16.680
Mr. Ido!

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:18.410
Ms. Karla, stop them!

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.120
I'm sorry, I can't.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:20.960
Stop your fire!

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:21.360
Hold it right there!

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.620
We'll only be hitting each other!

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:25.540
Return to defensive formation!

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:29.000
Switch your sensors to IR mode!

00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:30.960
Don't shoot, you idiots!

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.130
You'll hit friendlies!

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.400
Stand back!

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:34.550
Y-Yeah...

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:46.560
Thank goodness, Mr. Ido.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:49.110
Isn't it ironic, Karla.

00:18:49.110 --> 00:18:52.480
That I was saved by the sensor
you've procured.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.280
You're there, I know. Come out!

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:09.170
My... body!

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.280
No way...

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:51.230
No, it's true. But how...

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:53.440
So you're Kain Arisugawa?

00:20:53.440 --> 00:21:00.030
That's correct. Kain Arisugawa is what I'm
called and I recognize myself as such.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:01.900
And I also perform the duties as so.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.750
That's one roundabout way of talking.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:10.160
Tell me everything you know about the wandering planet Rajeev.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:15.630
And tell me who's Alice, the girl that
appeared from inside the planet?

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:21.670
Karla's intel was spot on, you've really lost your entire memories.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:26.470
If you still had them, you would have came here right away.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:29.470
You know who I am, don't you?

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:33.310
Yeah, I know, and disgustingly well,
I could say.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.610
But how did you escape
from that exile ship?

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:37.510
I'm asking the question!

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:39.650
Answer me. Tell me who I am!

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:46.510
An I-Machine longing for its memories
so much it became an Evertrancer.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:49.180
What a pitiful being, isn't it...

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:52.450
But I don't feel pity for you.
I don't need to.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:57.000
Because without your memories
you're worthless.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:22:00.210
I didn't even need to bring
you all the way here.

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:03.830
Seriously, what a waste of effort.

00:22:08.270 --> 00:22:09.380
What happened?

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:11.010
That jump of consciousness.

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:13.270
MT System?

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:14.650
That's correct.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:19.170
The mask I'm wearing is
not to hide my face.

00:22:19.690 --> 00:22:24.980
That's the state of the art portable Mind Trance System my company has developed.

00:22:26.050 --> 00:22:29.050
Step away.
I'll have to be a bit rough.

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:30.320
Please, Ido's...

00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:32.160
I've told you to step away.

00:22:35.500 --> 00:22:37.890
If you're telling me to fight,
I don't mind.

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:41.040
But answer my question.
Who am I?!

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:47.260
If you're so insistent,
I'll tell you the truth.

00:22:47.890 --> 00:22:52.760
The body lying over there should have been originally yours.

00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:53.680
What?

00:22:54.310 --> 00:22:55.470
That means...

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:59.710
You've already met Kain Arisugawa
before coming here.

00:22:59.710 --> 00:23:01.260
Shouldn't it be obvious?!

00:23:01.260 --> 00:23:04.380
You yourself are Kain!

00:23:04.380 --> 00:23:06.860
Kain... is me?

00:23:06.860 --> 00:23:12.550
Aah, the day of reunion! To think the day I can start over has come!

00:23:12.550 --> 00:23:15.610
I'm! I'm!

00:23:17.400 --> 00:23:21.130
I'm delighted, Kain Arisugawa.

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:29.410
Traveling as punishment,
or wandering in silence.

00:23:29.410 --> 00:23:34.220
Beyond the endless empty space there's a void full of luster.

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:39.810
When I stand at that place, the light of wickedness dries my tears.
